<title>AUSTRALIA: Australia petroleum refinery output rises in Jan.</title>
<headline>Australia petroleum refinery output rises in Jan.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's petroleum refinery production rose to 3,774.4 megalitres in January from 3,671.9 in December and 3,568.8 megalitres a year earlier, the Department of Primary Industries and Energy said on Friday.</p>
<p>Refinery input rose to 3,968.4 megalitres, of which 40.9 percent was indigenous, in January from 3,829.9 (41.8 percent) in December and 3,701.7 (45.4 percent) in January 1996, the department said in its Australian Petroleum Statistics bulletin.</p>
<p>NOTE: One megalitre equals 6,290 barrels.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
